{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/pulls/22311","id":2793629313,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAwRO586mg2aB","html_url":"https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/pull/22311","diff_url":"https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/pull/22311.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/pull/22311.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/issues/22311","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/pulls/22311/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/pulls/22311/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/issues/22311/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/statuses/4df55b353dc43e19738e9668e2344d25e46f40e0","number":22311,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Full Multi-Architecture Enablement for Harbor (amd64 + arm64)","user":{"login":"ranimandepudi","id":66872302,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2ODcyMzAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66872302?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi","html_url":"https://github.com/ranimandepudi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranimandepudi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR completes the multi-architecture enablement for Harbor. It builds on [#22229](https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/pull/22229) and expands it from CI-only coverage into full tooling, release plumbing, and multi-arch image publishing.\r\n\r\n### Changes:\r\n\r\n**Step 1: CI Matrix:** \r\n\r\n- Updated .github/workflows/CI.yml to run all PR test jobs on both amd64 and arm64.\r\n- Added strategy.matrix.arch: [amd64, arm64] for jobs:\r\nUTTEST\r\nAPITEST_DB\r\nAPITEST_DB_PROXY_CACHE\r\nAPITEST_LDAP\r\nOFFLINE\r\nUI_UT\r\n- amd64 jobs continue unchanged on ubuntu-latest.\r\n- arm64 jobs run on GitHub-hosted ubuntu-24.04-arm runners.\r\n- Exposed ARCH=${{ matrix.arch }} in the environment.\r\n- Codecov uploads are tagged by arch for clarity.\r\n\r\n**Step 2: Tooling Neutrality:**\r\n\r\n- tools/migrate_chart: Dockerfile + Python entrypoint updated to select correct Helm binary for both amd64 and arm64.\r\n- tools/spectral: Dockerfile updated to download correct Spectral binary per arch.\r\n- tests/test-engine-image/Dockerfile.common: added arch-awareness for containerd, helm, ORAS, wasm-to-oci, cosign, imgpkg, notation. On arm64, wasm-to-oci is built from source.\r\n- Ensures all helper/tooling images work natively on both architectures.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Step 3: Release Plumbing:**\r\n\r\n- Updated .github/workflows/build-package.yml to produce both amd64 and arm64 installers.\r\n- Updated .github/workflows/publish_release.yml to handle per-arch offline/online bundles.\r\n- Patched tools/release/release_utils.sh to push per-arch image tags (-amd64, -arm64).\r\n- docker_compose.py updated to render platform: linux/amd64 or linux/arm64 dynamically.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Step 4: Multi-Arch Image Publishing:**\r\n\r\n- In publish_release.yml, added docker buildx imagetools create per-arch images into unified multi-arch manifests.\r\n- Harbor component images (core, jobservice, registryctl, portal, etc.) are now published under a single tag (goharbor/<component>:vX.Y.Z) that transparently resolves to the right arch.\r\n- Mirrors existing Harbor release process: no user-facing change except that arm64 is now supported equally.\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior:\r\n\r\nPR CI runs on both amd64 and arm64; all jobs pass (offline + online).\r\nOffline and online installers are produced for both arches.\r\ndocker pull goharbor/core:<tag> resolves automatically to the native image on amd64 or arm64.\r\nDevelopers can build and run Harbor from source on arm64 using:\r\n`make compile`\r\n`make build -e VERSIONTAG=dev -e BASEIMAGETAG=dev -e PULL_BASE_FROM_DOCKERHUB=false -e PUSHBASEIMAGE=false -e BUILD_BASE=true -e TRIVYFLAG=true -e BUILDTRIVYADP=true`\r\n\r\n### RoadMap Discussed: \r\n\r\nStep 1: CI coverage \r\nStep 2: Tooling Neutrality \r\nStep 3: Release Plumbing \r\nStep 4: Multi-Arch image publishing \r\n\r\nWith this PR, Harbor achieves full parity on amd64 and arm64, covering source builds, CI, release workflows, and published images.\r\n\r\n### Thanks\r\nThanks to the Harbor maintainers and community for reviewing this. This contribution ensures Harbor is production-ready on modern Arm platforms, aligning with CNCF best practices for multi-arch support.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":4030991378,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAwRO587wRAwS","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/labels/release-note/new-feature","name":"release-note/new-feature","description":"New Harbor Feature","color":"DB7605","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4030996843,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAwRO587wRCFr","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/labels/release-note/infra","name":"release-note/infra","description":"Infra related changes e.g. release, test, ship etc...","color":"E846FD","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10073596414,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAwRO588AAAACWG7h_g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goharbor/harbor/labels/target/2.16.0","name":"target/2.16.0","description":"","color":"b60205","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"miles